BROWSER PROBE — RAN FOR REAL, PASSED
The repo has no Makefile/CI wiring for PLAYWRIGHT_MODULE; the convention is
standalone .cjs probes run with env vars (internal/handlers/whatif/testdata/
guardrail_ranges_browser.cjs, roth_apply_browser.cjs). I resolved a real
toolchain and ran it:
  PLAYWRIGHT_MODULE=/home/darrell/.npm/_npx/9833c18b2d85bc59/node_modules/playwright
  CHROMIUM_EXECUTABLE=/home/darrell/.cache/ms-playwright/chromium-1243/chrome-linux64/chrome
  go test -count=1 -v -timeout=300s -run TestGuardrailChartToneContrastBrowser ./cmd/server/
Result: `--- PASS: TestGuardrailChartToneContrastBrowser (16.63s)` /
`ok budget2/cmd/server 16.641s` / EXIT=0. NOT a skip — the log shows a real
Chromium session against an isolated :0 server (port 34059), a live plotly
fetch, GET /whatif/chart/projection 200, theme toggle and tab switches.
Mutation-kill of the probe itself:
- charts.js themechange tone restyle disabled -> probe FAILS with
  'dark: "Planned" contrast 1.99:1 vs card bg rgb(41,37,36) — want >= 3:1'.
- run against BASE 5fae968 (probe files copied in, no GV2 code) -> FAILS with
  'guardrails were not enabled on the seeded test settings — fixture defect',
  i.e. the probe cannot pass on a featureless tree.
Additional throwaway probe (mine, discarded): loading /whatif with
localStorage theme=dark set BEFORE navigation renders the legend swatches
already in the dark palette (rgb(248,113,113) etc.); with the on-render
`applyTonePalette(data.data, getTonePalette())` call removed the swatch is
rgb(220,38,38) — so criterion 6(c)'s on-render half is proved to execute.
Harness gaps disclosed: this is a real Chromium, so no jsdom caveats apply;
prefers-color-scheme is not exercised (theme comes from localStorage), and
the probe reads legend swatches rather than the plotted strokes themselves.

